(1) To implement policies, strategies, master plans, programs, measures, and guidelines for the promotion and development of families and the protection of welfare;
(2) To provide knowledge and understanding, consultation and advice, and mediation and conciliation in matters of family problems, as well as to receive notifications, collect, and compile facts concerning acts of domestic violence for the benefit of filing petitions or statements to the court and the protection of welfare;
(3) To serve as a learning center for the promotion and development of families and the protection of welfare, and to serve as a coordination center with government agencies and the private sector in carrying out operations to promote and develop families and protect welfare;
(4) To carry out the protection of welfare, or to file petitions or statements to the court to carry out the protection of welfare, as well as to implement court orders or orders of the head of the center for the protection of welfare;
(5) To implement programs and guidelines for the development of the capacity of officials and personnel involved in the promotion and development of families and the protection of welfare, as well as to evaluate the performance of officials and personnel in the Family Promotion and Protection Center;
(6) To monitor and report the results of operations under this Act to the Director-General and the Minister;
(7) To provide assistance or relief to families in difficult circumstances in accordance with regulations prescribed by the Minister;
(8) To promote and support the solicitation of opinions and constructive exchange of learning by families or representatives of families, in order to lead to the determination of policies, strategies, master plans, programs, measures, and guidelines for the promotion and development of families and the protection of welfare by the Committee in the future;
(9) To carry out any other operations concerning the promotion and development of families and the protection of welfare as provided in this Act and under other laws, or as assigned by the Committee or the Department of Women's Affairs and Family Development.

Chapter 5 Promotion and Development of Families

Section 17

For the benefit of the promotion and development of families, the Department of Women's Affairs and Family Development shall coordinate with the Ministry of Interior to ensure that registrars under the law on family registration, government officials performing duties related to the promotion and development of families, CFDCs, or private organizations having objectives in the promotion and development of families have knowledge and understanding in the promotion and development of families.

Volume 136 Part 67 Kor	Government Gazette	22 May 2019

In carrying out operations under paragraph one to provide knowledge and understanding in the promotion and development of families, such knowledge shall include the following:
(1) Knowledge concerning the relationship between husband and wife, property between husband and wife, the validity of marriage, the termination of marriage, parentage with children, the rights and duties of parents and children, adopted children, maintenance, as well as matters of inheritance and wills;
(2) Knowledge concerning the protection of welfare, or other knowledge relating to families and the institution of the family;
(3) Knowledge and skills in choosing a spouse, married life, emotional changes and emotional control;
(4) Knowledge in preparing before and after pregnancy, knowledge and skills in raising children;
(5) Knowledge in pursuing occupations, creating jobs and income, saving, managing property, and accessing sources of capital for pursuing occupations to support families;
(6) Knowledge of the rights and duties of citizenship, rights and welfare, and guidelines for requesting assistance from government agencies or private organizations;
(7) Any other knowledge concerning the promotion and development of families.
In carrying out operations under paragraphs one and two, the Department of Women's Affairs and Family Development shall carry out operations to achieve cooperation and coordination among various agencies in order to achieve integration of the promotion and development of the institution of the family.
